# Virtual Environment Directories - More Specific
**/env*/
**/.env/
**/venv*/
**/numpy_env/
**/tensorflow_env/
**/env1/

# Specific Script Directories to Ignore
**/Scripts/
**/activate*
**/deactivate*
**/pip*.exe
**/python*.exe

# Python Virtual Environment Files
*.cfg
*.pyproj
*.sln

# Database and Large Files
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*SemanticSymbols.db
**/CopilotIndices/**
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
**/*.h5
**/*.bin

# VS Code specific
**/.vs/
**/FileContentIndex/
**/*.vsidx
**/*.wsuo
**/DocumentLayout*.json
**/copilot-chat/
# Secrets — credentials, API keys, private keys.
# NOTE: the "**/.env/" rule above has a trailing slash, so it only matches a
# DIRECTORY named .env. It does NOT ignore a .env FILE. These rules do.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
!cacert.pem
*.key
secrets.json

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
